@@ -7,6 +7,36 @@ Whenever anyone from a different API server talks in chat, fallback API server p

 ## My game immediately crashed!

+If you're getting a crash on Android or a non-standard JVM like this:
+
+```
+#  SIGSEGV (0xb) at pc=0x..., pid=..., tid=...
+# Problematic frame:
+# C  [libinstrument.so+0x...]
+```
+
+then the JVM's class retransformation implementation has crashed. This is a known issue
+with Android-based JVMs (ZalithLauncher2, PojavLauncher, etc.) on aarch64. To work around
+this, add the following JVM argument:
+
+```
+-DLoki.no_retransform=true
+```
+
+This disables retransformation of already-loaded classes. The following features will not
+apply to classes that were already loaded before Loki started:
+
+- **Authlib-Injector killer** -- authlib-injector classes already loaded will not be
+  neutralised. Simply do not use authlib-injector on Android.
+- **Forge 1.13-1.16 URL factory fix** -- the LegacyFix agent's URL factory override will
+  not be intercepted. Forge does not run on Android.
+- **DNS blocking** -- `InetAddress` DNS lookups for blocked hosts (OptiFine, snooper) will
+  not be intercepted. Snooper and OptiFine cape blocking are handled by Loki's URL factory,
+  which continues to work.
+
+WebSocket signaling support for Minecraft 26.2+ official multiplayer is **not** affected
+by this option.
+
